#MANUAL
ie.manual.category.engineered_schematics.name=Engineered Schematics
ie.manual.entry.es.name=Introduction
ie.manual.entry.es.subtext=Projecting the Future
ie.manual.entry.es0=Greetings and welcome to Engineered Schematics.<br><br>Engineered Schematics is designed to be the ultimate building companion for players using Immersive Engineering and its many add-ons.<br><br>This mod provides a detailed guide to constructing complex multiblock machines, ensuring you build them quickly, accurately, and efficiently.
ie.manual.entry.es1=Whether you're a seasoned engineer or just getting started, Engineered Schematics will help you navigate these advanced builds with ease.<br>Let's <link;schematicTable;get started>.
ie.manual.entry.schematicTable.name=Schematic Table
ie.manual.entry.schematicTable.subtext=The Architect’s Codex
ie.manual.entry.schematicTable0=To begin, you'll need to craft a Schematic Table.<br>This table turns paper into a <link;schematicItem;schematic> for any multiblock structure registered with Immersive Engineering.
ie.manual.entry.schematicItem.name=Multiblock Schematic
ie.manual.entry.schematicItem.subtext=Block by Block
ie.manual.entry.schematicItem0=This guide explains how to use the Multiblock Schematic.<br>Follow the steps below to easily place, move, and build your multiblock structures with visual feedback.
ie.manual.entry.schematicItem1=§lPlace and Move:§r Right-click with the schematic in your MAIN hand to set or reposition the multiblock footprint.<br>§lRotate Multiblock:§r Sneak and right-click with the schematic in your MAIN hand to rotate the structure so that it faces you.<br>§lBuild Guide:§r Hold the schematic in your OFF hand to enable the build guide. When holding the correct block, matching positions highlight §lgreen§r. A wrongly placed block disables the guide and highlights §lred§r. Wrong orientation or state highlights §lyellow§r.
ie.manual.entry.schematicItem2=§lFormation Block:§r Once the structure is complete, the schematic shows the formation block to hit with a hammer.
